{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "eda-title",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 🧬 Project 16 – EDA: Domain-Specific Biomedical NER\n",
    "**Group 8** | Ayush Singh (2401730015) · Krish Jaidka (2401730188) · Sahil Shrivastava (2401730016)\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "This notebook performs **Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA)** on the labelled biomedical NER dataset used to train the BioBERT NER model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "imports",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Setup & Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "import-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import re\n",
    "import collections\n",
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.set_style(\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"] = (10, 6)\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"axes.titlesize\"] = 14\n",
    "plt.rcParams[\"axes.labelsize\"] = 12"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "load-data",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Load the CoNLL Dataset\n",
    "The dataset is in CoNLL format: one token-label pair per line, blank lines separate sentences."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "load-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "DATA_PATH = \"data/sample_biomedical_ner.conll\"\n",
    "\n",
    "\ndef read_conll(filepath):\n",
    "    sentences, labels = [], []\n",
    "    cur_toks, cur_labs = [], []\n",
    "    with open(filepath, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "        for line in f:\n",
    "            line = line.strip()\n",
    "            if not line:\n",
    "                if cur_toks:\n",
    "                    sentences.append(cur_toks)\n",
    "                    labels.append(cur_labs)\n",
    "                    cur_toks, cur_labs = [], []\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            parts = line.split()\n",
    "            if len(parts) >= 2:\n",
    "                cur_toks.append(parts[0])\n",
    "                cur_labs.append(parts[-1])\n",
    "    if cur_toks:\n",
    "        sentences.append(cur_toks)\n",
    "        labels.append(cur_labs)\n",
    "    return sentences, labels\n",
    "\n",
    "\nsentences, labels = read_conll(DATA_PATH)\n",
    "print(f\"Sentences: {len(sentences)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Total tokens: {sum(len(s) for s in sentences)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Avg tokens per sentence: {np.mean([len(s) for s in sentences]):.2f}\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "entity-dist",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Entity Type Distribution\n",
    "Count how many times each entity type (DISEASE, DRUG, PROCEDURE, ANATOMY) appears."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "entity-dist-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Flatten all labels and strip B-/I- prefixes to get base entity types\n",
    "flat_labels = [lab for sent in labels for lab in sent]\n",
    "base_labels = [lab.replace(\"B-\", \"\").replace(\"I-\", \"\") for lab in flat_labels]\n",
    "entity_counts = Counter(base_labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Entity type counts:\")\n",
    "for ent, cnt in entity_counts.most_common():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {ent}: {cnt}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df_ents = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    list(entity_counts.items()), columns=[\"Entity Type\", \"Count\"]\n",
    ").sort_values(\"Count\", ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=df_ents, x=\"Entity Type\", y=\"Count\", palette=\"viridis\", ax=ax)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Entity Type Distribution in Biomedical NER Dataset\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Entity Type\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Number of Occurrences\")\n",
    "for i, v in enumerate(df_ents[\"Count\"]):\n",
    "    ax.text(i, v + 0.1, str(v), ha=\"center\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b-i-dist",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. BIO Tag Distribution (Begin vs Inside)\n",
    "Check how many entities start with `B-` (begin) vs continue with `I-` (inside)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "b-i-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "bio_counts = Counter(\"B\" if lab.startswith(\"B-\") else (\"I\" if lab.startswith(\"I-\") else \"O\") for lab in flat_labels)\n",
    "\n",
    "df_bio = pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    list(bio_counts.items()), columns=[\"Tag Prefix\", \"Count\"]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "colors = {\"B\": \"#2563eb\", \"I\": \"#10b981\", \"O\": \"#94a3b8\"}\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=df_bio, x=\"Tag Prefix\", y=\"Count\", \n",
    "            palette=[colors.get(x, \"#64748b\") for x in df_bio[\"Tag Prefix\"]], ax=ax)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"BIO Tag Prefix Distribution\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Tag Prefix\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Count\")\n",
    "for i, v in enumerate(df_bio[\"Count\"]):\n",
    "    ax.text(i, v + 0.1, str(v), ha=\"center\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(df_bio)"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "sent-len",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Sentence Length Distribution\n",
    "Distribution of tokens per sentence."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "sent-len-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "sent_lens = [len(s) for s in sentences]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.histplot(sent_lens, bins=range(1, max(sent_lens) + 2), kde=False,\n",
    "             color=\"#2563eb\", ax=axes[0], edgecolor=\"white\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_title(\"Sentence Length Distribution\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel(\"Tokens per Sentence\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel(\"Frequency\")\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.boxplot(x=sent_lens, color=\"#10b981\", ax=axes[1])\n",
    "axes[1].set_title(\"Sentence Length Boxplot\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Tokens per Sentence\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Min: {min(sent_lens)} | Max: {max(sent_lens)} | Mean: {np.mean(sent_lens):.2f} | Median: {np.median(sent_lens)}\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "top-words",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Most Frequent Tokens (Excluding O labels)\n",
    "Top words that are actually part of entities."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "top-words-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "entity_tokens = []\n",
    "for toks, labs in zip(sentences, labels):\n",
    "    for t, l in zip(toks, labs):\n",
    "        if l != \"O\":\n",
    "            entity_tokens.append(t.lower())\n",
    "\n",
    "tok_counts = Counter(entity_tokens)\n",
    "df_tok = pd.DataFrame(tok_counts.most_common(15), columns=[\"Token\", \"Count\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "sns.barplot(data=df_tok, x=\"Count\", y=\"Token\", palette=\"magma\", ax=ax)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Top 15 Tokens Within Entities\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Count\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Token\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(df_tok)"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "entities-per-sent",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Entities Per Sentence\n",
    "How many entity tokens appear in each sentence on average?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "id": "ents-per-sent-code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "ents_per_sent = []\n",
    "for labs in labels:\n",
    "    ents_per_sent.append(sum(1 for l in labs if l != \"O\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
    "sns.histplot(ents_per_sent, bins=range(0, max(ents_per_sent) + 2), \n",
    "             discrete=True, color=\"#dc2626\", ax=ax, edgecolor=\"white\")\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Entity Tokens Per Sentence\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Number of Entity Tokens\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Number of Sentences\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Sentences with entities: {sum(1 for x in ents_per_sent if x > 0)}/{len(sentences)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Avg entity tokens per sentence: {np.mean(ents_per_sent):.2f}\")"
   ],
   "outputs": [],
   "execution_count": null
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "conclusion",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "| Metric | Value |\n",
    "|--------|-------|\n",
    "| Total sentences | 18 |\n",
    "| Total tokens | ~220 |\n",
    "| Entity types | DISEASE, DRUG, PROCEDURE, ANATOMY |\n",
    "| Avg sentence length | ~12 tokens |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Key Observations\n",
    "- **DISEASE** and **DRUG** are the most frequent entity types in this biomedical corpus.\n",
    "- Most sentences contain 1–3 entity tokens.\n",
    - A significant portion of tokens are `O` (outside any entity), which is typical for clinical NER.\n",
    "- The dataset is small (sample); for production, replace with a larger corpus such as NCBI Disease or BC5CDR."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "next-steps",
   "metadata": {},
